window.AB900_TESTS = [{"t":"AB-900 Practice Exam #1","d":"48 scenario-based questions across all three AB-900 domains: identity & core services, data protection & governance, and Copilot & agent administration.","q":[["A new help desk technician only needs to reset passwords for locked-out users. Following least privilege, which role should you assign?",["Global Administrator","Password Administrator","Exchange Administrator","Compliance Administrator"],1,"Password Administrator (or Helpdesk Administrator) grants exactly the rights needed to reset passwords, without access to mailboxes or security policies. Global Admin should be reserved for emergencies."],["A user was denied access this morning. Which tool shows you exactly which Conditional Access policy blocked the sign-in?",["What If tool","Message center","Entra sign-in logs","Usage reports"],2,"Sign-in logs record what actually happened: who, when, where, and which policy applied. The What If tool simulates what WOULD happen."],["You want to see which Conditional Access policies would apply to a specific user signing in from a specific location, without the user actually signing in. What do you use?",["What If tool","Sign-in logs","Identity Secure Score","Activity explorer"],0,"The What If tool is the 'flight simulator' for Conditional Access: it simulates a sign-in to show which policies apply and whether access would be granted."],["A heavily regulated organization with on-premises Active Directory requires that passwords are NEVER stored in the cloud in any form. Which hybrid authentication method fits?",["Password Hash Synchronization (PHS)","Pass-Through Authentication (PTA)","Cloud-only identities","Self-service password reset"],1,"With PTA, an on-premises agent validates the password against local AD in real time; no password or hash is stored in Entra ID. PHS syncs a hash to the cloud."],["Which hybrid authentication method is Microsoft's most common recommendation and still lets users sign in if on-premises servers go down?",["Federation with AD FS","Pass-Through Authentication","Password Hash Synchronization","Certificate-based authentication"],2,"PHS syncs a cryptographic hash to Entra ID and validates in the cloud, so it is simple and resilient. PTA and Federation both depend on on-prem infrastructure being available."],["A project team needs a shared mailbox, group calendar, SharePoint document library and Planner board created automatically. Which group type should you create?",["Security group","Distribution group","Mail-enabled security group","Microsoft 365 group"],3,"A Microsoft 365 group automatically provisions a shared mailbox, calendar, SharePoint library, Planner and optionally a Team. Security groups only control access; distribution groups only send email."],["You want users to be added to the Sales group automatically when HR sets their department attribute to 'Sales', and removed when it changes. What should you use?",["Dynamic group","Distribution group","Access package","Nested security group"],0,"Dynamic groups populate automatically from user attributes in Entra ID (e.g. department = Sales), with zero manual admin work."],["Where do you configure OneDrive sync behavior, sharing permissions and storage limits?",["The OneDrive admin center","The SharePoint admin center","The Exchange admin center","The Teams admin center"],1,"Classic exam trap: there is no separate OneDrive admin portal. OneDrive is built on SharePoint, so its settings live in the SharePoint admin center."],["Many users suddenly report that email isn't working. What should you check FIRST?",["Each user's license assignment","Mail flow rules in the Exchange admin center","The Service health dashboard","The Message center"],2,"Always rule out a Microsoft-side outage first via Service health. Then communicate with users, verify your own config (e.g. with Exchange Online PowerShell), and document afterwards."],["Where would you find guidance about a new Teams meeting policy that Microsoft is rolling out next month?",["Service health dashboard","Usage reports","Message center","Sign-in logs"],2,"Message center = upcoming changes. Service health = current incidents and outages. Usage reports = adoption metrics."],["Your company is being sued and legal needs ALL mailbox data, including deleted items and original versions, preserved indefinitely. What do you apply?",["A 30-day retention policy","Litigation hold","A DLP policy","A sensitivity label"],1,"Retention = housekeeping. Litigation hold = a legal freeze that preserves everything indefinitely for legal discovery."],["You want to collaborate with an external partner on one project inside Teams without giving them access to the whole team. Which channel type?",["Standard channel","Private channel","Shared channel","Announcement channel"],2,"Shared channels act as a bridge to people in other departments or external organizations without granting access to the entire team. Private channels restrict access to a subset of the team."],["Which Defender XDR component detects pass-the-hash and lateral movement by monitoring on-premises Active Directory?",["Defender for Office 365","Defender for Endpoint","Defender for Identity","Defender for Cloud Apps"],2,"Defender for Identity monitors on-prem AD signals and bridges the visibility gap in hybrid environments."],["A malicious email got past filters and was delivered. Minutes later Microsoft identifies the threat and removes the message from the mailbox. What feature did this?",["Safe Links","Zero-hour Auto Purge (ZAP)","Transport rules","Spoof intelligence"],1,"ZAP retroactively removes malicious messages AFTER delivery when new threat intelligence identifies them."],["Employees read work email on personal phones. You must stop them copying corporate data from Outlook into personal apps WITHOUT enrolling or managing the whole device. What do you use?",["Device compliance policies","App protection policies","Security defaults","Retention policies"],1,"App protection policies secure data at the application level, which makes them ideal for BYOD, without full device management."],["A healthcare company wants a score showing how well its configuration meets HIPAA requirements, with improvement actions. Which tool?",["Microsoft Secure Score","Identity Secure Score","Purview Compliance Manager","Usage reports"],2,"Compliance Manager maps configuration against external regulations (HIPAA, GDPR, ISO 27001). Secure Score measures internal security posture against best practices."],["You want users on unmanaged home PCs to view SharePoint files in the browser but NOT download or print them. What enforces this?",["Conditional Access session controls via Defender for Cloud Apps","A retention label","Defender for Identity","Self-service password reset"],0,"Session controls grant access but limit what users can do during the session; they are enforced through Defender for Cloud Apps."],["Defender for Endpoint automatically isolates a laptop showing ransomware behavior. Which Zero Trust principle does this best represent?",["Verify explicitly","Use least privilege access","Assume breach","Trusted network"],2,"Assume breach shifts the mindset from prevention to rapid containment: detect, isolate and contain."],["You need to automatically delete ALL Teams chats older than 90 days across the entire company, regardless of content. What do you use?",["A retention label","A retention policy","A sensitivity label","Litigation hold"],1,"Labels apply to items; policies apply to locations. A retention policy broadly targets a location such as all Teams chats."],["Your DLP policy keeps flagging 9-digit inventory part numbers as ID numbers. HR can provide a file of the actual employee IDs. What reduces false positives most?",["Regex pattern matching","Exact Data Match (EDM)","Trainable classifiers","Retention labels"],1,"EDM triggers only on exact matches against a secure list your organization uploads: the 'VIP guest list' versus regex's guessing."],["You want Purview to recognize résumés even when the word 'resume' never appears. What do you use, and roughly how many samples does it need at minimum?",["Sensitive info types, 5 samples","Trainable classifiers, 50 samples","EDM, 500 samples","Regex, 1 sample"],1,"Trainable classifiers use machine learning and need at least 50 sample documents to learn a category without a predictable pattern."],["A confidential report is downloaded to a USB drive and emailed outside the company, yet it still cannot be opened by unauthorized people. What provides this protection?",["A DLP policy","A retention policy","A sensitivity label with encryption","A transport rule"],2,"Sensitivity labels embed protection (encryption via Azure Rights Management) in the file's metadata, so it travels with the file everywhere."],["An employee submits a resignation and then downloads 50 confidential files at 3 AM. Which Purview solution correlates the HR signal with the behavior?",["Communication Compliance","Insider Risk Management","eDiscovery Standard","Compliance Manager"],1,"Insider Risk Management combines user activity with HR signals to determine when a risk threshold is crossed."],["A financial firm must detect insider-trading language and harassment in Teams messages, emails and Copilot chats, with human review. Which solution?",["Communication Compliance","Insider Risk Management","DLP","Activity explorer"],0,"Communication Compliance scans what people say (including Copilot chats) with ML classifiers and routes flags to human reviewers."],["What distinguishes Activity explorer from a standard alerts dashboard?",["It only shows policy violations","It shows all user and data activity as a timeline, even when no policy was violated","It deletes risky files automatically","It calculates the compliance score"],1,"Activity explorer provides a forensic, chronological view of all activity (labeled → USB → shared externally), and is the starting point for triage."],["High-risk users (per Insider Risk Management) get strict DLP blocks, while low-risk users only see policy tips. What is this called?",["Adaptive Protection","Endpoint DLP","Auto-labeling","Conditional Access"],0,"Adaptive Protection dynamically links Insider Risk Management risk levels to DLP enforcement."],["Legal needs case management, review sets, near-duplicate detection and redaction. Which edition?",["Content search","eDiscovery Standard","eDiscovery Premium","Compliance Manager"],2,"Standard covers search, export and holds. Premium adds case management, review sets, analytics (near-duplicates) and redaction."],["You discover many employees paste company data into unapproved third-party generative AI apps. Which Purview capability gives visibility into this 'shadow AI'?",["DSPM for AI","eDiscovery","Compliance Manager","Retention policies"],0,"DSPM for AI monitors AI interactions and shadow AI usage. Shadow IT → Defender for Cloud Apps; Shadow AI → DSPM for AI."],["Which report in the SharePoint admin center flags sites with sensitive content shared too broadly, sites with inactive owners, and sites missing sensitivity labels?",["Usage reports","Data Access Governance (DAG) reports","Sign-in logs","Message center"],1,"DAG reports are the primary roadmap for targeted oversharing remediation."],["You need to force site owners to periodically confirm who still needs access, and get alerts on stale inactive sites. Which paid add-on provides this?",["Defender for Office 365 Plan 2","SharePoint Advanced Management (SAM)","Viva Insights","Entra ID P1"],1,"SAM adds restricted site access, inactivity alerts and site access reviews."],["A marketing user asks Copilot to summarize a finance report stored in a SharePoint folder restricted to the finance team. What happens?",["Copilot summarizes it but hides numbers","Copilot returns nothing; to that user, the file effectively doesn't exist","Copilot asks the finance team for approval","Copilot summarizes it because AI bypasses permissions"],1,"The golden rule: Copilot only sees what the user can see. Microsoft Graph checks permissions using the user's token."],["Before a broad Copilot rollout, you find many sites shared with 'Everyone'. According to the Prepare/Operate model, what should you do first?",["Roll out Copilot and monitor DLP alerts later","Fix and restrict existing oversharing risks before broad rollout","Disable SharePoint entirely","Give every user eDiscovery Premium"],1,"Prepare = fix existing risks first (restrict access, DAG reports, labels, e.g. Restricted SharePoint Search). Operate = monitor for new risks."],["Which describes an AGENT rather than Copilot?",["Waits for the user to type a prompt in Word","Runs every night, triggered on schedule, often under its own service account","Only uses the signed-in user's identity","Summarizes the email you currently have open"],1,"Copilot is interactive and reactive ('the UI for AI'); agents can be autonomous, triggered by schedules or events, and often use service accounts or managed identities."],["In Copilot's architecture, what does 'grounding' mean?",["Training the public LLM on your tenant's data","Enriching the user's prompt with relevant, authorized organizational data from Microsoft Graph before sending it to the LLM","Blocking Copilot during an outage","Encrypting data at rest"],1,"The orchestrator enriches the prompt with Graph/Work IQ context (a grounded prompt). Tenant data never trains public foundation models."],["A 20-person firm uses only free Microsoft 365 Copilot Chat and can't get it to summarize internal project files. Why?",["Free Copilot Chat is web-grounded only; they need a paid Microsoft 365 Copilot license for Graph data","Their SharePoint is too small","They must enable eDiscovery","Copilot never reads internal files"],0,"Free Copilot Chat has no access to your organization's Graph data. The paid Microsoft 365 Copilot license grounds responses in emails, chats and files."],["You created a pay-as-you-go billing policy with a $500 budget, but users still can't use the pay-as-you-go service. What step was most likely missed?",["Assigning Global Admin","Connecting the billing policy to the specific service on the Pay-as-you-go services tab","Setting the alert at 100%","Enabling security defaults"],1,"Step 1: create the billing policy. Step 2: connect it to the service. Without step 2, pay-as-you-go stays disabled by default."],["You need to group Copilot pay-as-you-go costs by user principal name and export them to Power BI. Which tool?",["Microsoft 365 admin center billing","Azure Cost Management","Message center","Viva Engage"],1,"M365 admin center = invoices and license counts (summary). Azure Cost Management = deep analytics, group by, forecasting, alerts and export to CSV/Power BI."],["A licensed user can't see Copilot in Word. Service health is fine. What is the most common cause?",["They aren't running Microsoft 365 Apps for enterprise (or it's outdated)","Their mailbox is full","DLP is blocking Word","They are in a dynamic group"],0,"Check File → Account → Product information shows Microsoft 365 Apps for enterprise, then Update options → Update now."],["Copilot meeting recaps can't be generated for the HR department in Teams. What is the likely cause?",["HR lacks an E5 license","Meeting transcription is disabled for HR","HR uses shared channels","The Message center is turned off"],1,"Underlying dependency: Copilot in Teams requires meeting transcription to be allowed."],["What is the maximum number of starter prompts for a SharePoint agent?",["1","3","20","Unlimited"],1,"SharePoint agents: 3 starter prompts, up to 20 sources, welcome message supported, no code interpreter or image generator. Copilot Studio agents: unlimited starter prompts."],["Which agent can you NOT edit?",["A custom SharePoint agent stored as a .agent file","A Copilot Studio agent you created","The ready-made agent automatically created for a SharePoint site","A shared agent you own"],2,"The ready-made site agent is locked. To change its scope, create a custom agent (like the Contoso Mega 300 example)."],["You spent 20 minutes refining an agent in the Describe tab, then selected a new template in the Configure tab. What happens?",["Your refinements are merged with the template","The configuration resets to the template defaults, overwriting your refinements","Nothing, templates only apply to new agents","Copilot Studio asks clarifying questions"],1,"Applying a template in Configure performs a hard reset to that template's defaults."],["What is the maximum number of knowledge sources for an agent?",["5","10","20","100"],2,"Both Copilot Studio (Lite) agents and SharePoint agents cap at 20 knowledge sources."],["Following least privilege, which role should review and approve requested agents in the Microsoft 365 admin center?",["Global Administrator","AI Administrator","Exchange Administrator","Billing Administrator"],1,"Use the AI Administrator role (or Global Reader for view-only). Reserve Global Admin for emergencies."],["You plan to retire a widely used agent. What is the recommended minimum advance notice to impacted users?",["24 hours","7 days","30 days","No notice needed"],2,"Communicate retirement at least 30 days in advance and provide training for the replacement tool."],["A department head asks which quarter had the highest variance between forecast and actual expenses in a spreadsheet. Which prebuilt agent fits best?",["Researcher","Analyst","Writing Coach","Ideas Coach"],1,"Researcher = unstructured text (emails, chats, docs). Analyst = structured data (spreadsheets, tables), no DAX needed."],["You checked Copilot usage reports this morning, but yesterday afternoon's activity isn't showing. What explains this?",["Reports only update monthly","Usage reports have a 24–48 hour ingestion delay","Copilot was down","You need Viva Insights to see any usage"],1,"Plan your reporting cadence around the 24–48 hour ingestion delay; don't chase daily noise."],["An agent has read AND write access to a SharePoint library, but its job only requires reading documents. What should you do?",["Nothing, more access improves answers","Scale its permissions back to read-only","Give it Global Admin","Delete the library"],1,"This is an over-privileged agent, a security vulnerability. Apply least privilege: read-only."]]},{"t":"AB-900 Practice Exam #2: Common Traps","d":"28 questions on common traps, especially Purview tool selection and agent types.","q":[["In the Microsoft 365 admin center, where do you add and verify a new custom domain such as contoso.com?",["Settings > Org settings > Organization profile","Setup > Domains","Exchange admin center > Mail flow","Entra admin center > Enterprise applications"],1,"Domains are added and verified through the Domains area (reached via Setup in the official assessment). Organization profile does not manage domains, mail flow is for email routing, and Enterprise applications are for app management."],["Which statement describes AUTHORIZATION in Microsoft Entra?",["Proving who a user is by validating credentials","Creating a single sign-on session across apps","Determining what resources a verified identity can access and which actions it can perform","Encrypting data at rest"],2,"Authentication = who you are (ID check). Authorization = what you're allowed to do (the key card). SSO is a sign-in/session experience, which relates to authentication."],["Your compliance team wants Copilot and AI app prompts and responses kept for 1 year and then deleted automatically. What do you configure?",["Sensitive information types","A DLP policy","A retention policy","A sensitivity label"],2,"Retention policies control how long content (including supported AI prompts and responses) is kept and when it is deleted. SITs only identify sensitive patterns."],["After a file has been classified with a sensitivity label, how does the label continue to protect it?",["It tracks every sharing event for auditing","Its protection persists with the content wherever it is stored or shared","It identifies credit card patterns inside the file","It blocks all external sharing at the tenant level"],1,"Labels embed protection that travels with the file. Tracking actions = auditing/Activity explorer; identifying patterns = SITs; blocking sharing = DLP."],["Which Microsoft Purview feature detects sensitive information and PREVENTS it from being shared outside the company via email, SharePoint and OneDrive?",["Sensitivity labels","Retention labels","Data loss prevention (DLP) policies","Sharing policies"],2,"DLP is the 'airport baggage scanner' that stops sensitive data leaving. Sensitivity labels classify and protect the file itself."],["In Copilot Control System, which type of controls helps you monitor, detect and respond to risks from Copilot and agent use?",["Management controls","Compliance and privacy controls","AI security controls","Measurement and reporting"],2,"'Monitor, detect and respond to risks' is security language, so the answer is AI security controls. Compliance/privacy = regulatory requirements; management = operational governance like licenses."],["A DLP alert fires. You need to review the detailed user actions related to it. Which Purview tool is the primary investigation starting point?",["Microsoft Purview Audit","Content explorer","Activity explorer","Compliance Manager"],2,"Activity explorer shows user actions tied to DLP and labels. Content explorer shows WHERE sensitive data lives; Audit is broader logging, not the primary DLP investigation tool."],["You must assess and track compliance controls for your generative AI apps against the EU AI Act and NIST AI RMF. What does Compliance Manager provide?",["DLP enforcement on prompts","Regulatory templates and assessments to track compliance controls","Oversharing assessments for SharePoint","Capturing prompts in the audit log"],1,"Compliance Manager = regulatory templates and assessments (GDPR, HIPAA, EU AI Act, NIST AI RMF). Enforcement is DLP; oversharing is DSPM/DAG; logging is Audit."],["Before rolling out Copilot, you want to discover how employees are interacting with generative AI tools and spot data exposure risks. What do you use?",["DLP policies","Data Lifecycle Management","eDiscovery","DSPM for AI"],3,"DSPM for AI gives visibility into AI usage and exposure risks. DLP enforces, it doesn't discover how AI is being used."],["According to the official assessment, which SharePoint Advanced Management report surfaces unusual or potentially risky FILE ACCESS activity?",["Data access governance reports","Defender for Office 365 reports","Session summary reports","User risk reports in Entra"],2,"Session summary reports surface detailed activity and anomalies in file access. DAG reports focus on oversharing/exposure; Defender for Office 365 focuses on email threats; Entra risk reports focus on identity."],["You need tenant-wide insight into potential oversharing across all SharePoint and OneDrive sites before deploying Copilot. What should you use?",["Site access reviews","Data access governance (DAG) reports","Restricted Content Discovery","Change history reports"],1,"DAG reports give tenant-wide oversharing insight. Site access reviews are for remediating one specific site; Restricted Content Discovery hides content but doesn't identify oversharing."],["What does the 'Sharing links' Data access governance report show?",["Users who created the most sites","The largest files in SharePoint","Sites where the most sharing links were created in the last 28 days","SharePoint sign-in activity"],2,"The Sharing links DAG report highlights sites with the most sharing links created during the last 28 days."],["In the Microsoft PURVIEW portal (not SharePoint admin center), which feature identifies potential oversharing in SharePoint and OneDrive?",["Compliance Manager assessments","Data risk assessments (in DSPM)","DLP alerts","eDiscovery (Standard) cases"],1,"Data risk assessments in DSPM analyze permissions and exposure of sensitive data. SharePoint admin center = DAG reports; Purview portal = data risk assessments."],["You must limit a SharePoint site so ONLY members of specific Microsoft 365 groups or Entra security groups can access it. What do you use?",["Restricted access control","Data access governance reports","Block download policy","Site access reviews"],0,"Restricted access control (SAM) restricts site access to specified groups. Block download controls unmanaged-device actions; DAG reports discover; access reviews remediate."],["You need an agent that runs multi-step workflows in external systems with custom orchestration and your own AI models. Which agent type?",["Declarative agent","SharePoint agent","Custom engine agent","Copilot Prompt Gallery"],2,"Custom engine agents = custom orchestration, external systems, custom AI models. Declarative agents use Microsoft 365 data and Copilot's built-in orchestration."],["Which statement correctly describes a DECLARATIVE agent?",["It uses custom AI models and its own orchestration","It uses Microsoft 365 data and Copilot's built-in orchestration, without custom code","It only works in Teams chats","It requires Visual Studio Code to build"],1,"Declarative agents extend Copilot by declaring instructions, knowledge and actions, relying on Copilot's built-in orchestration. Custom engine agents bring their own orchestration and models."],["Leadership wants the Copilot Dashboard and the Advanced Insights Analyst Workbench for deep adoption analysis. What provides these?",["Microsoft 365 admin center usage reports","Power Platform and Copilot Studio analytics","Viva Insights Copilot Analytics","Purview audit logs"],2,"Viva Insights Copilot Analytics provides the Copilot Dashboard and the Advanced Insights Analyst Workbench. Power Platform analytics cover custom agents, not organization-wide Copilot adoption."],["When you create a pay-as-you-go billing policy for Copilot agents, which user-scoping options are available?",["All users or specific individual users","All users or a specific group","Only guest users","Up to 1,000 named users"],1,"PAYG billing policies scope to all users or a specific Microsoft Entra security group, not to individual user accounts."],["Following least privilege, which role can access Copilot > Billing & usage and configure pay-as-you-go billing?",["Exchange Administrator","SharePoint Administrator","AI Administrator","Teams Administrator"],2,"AI Administrator manages the Copilot node, including settings, agent approvals and PAYG billing, without full Global Admin rights."],["You need to delete several scheduled Copilot prompts created by another user. What must you do FIRST?",["Run the cleanup script","Get the Power Platform Administrator role","Install PowerShell modules","Connect to Azure"],1,"Scheduled prompts run through a Power Platform environment, so you need the Power Platform Administrator role before any script or module will work."],["A Security Copilot owner sets up a partner-built agent that requests permissions to Microsoft services like Entra ID and Sentinel. What must happen before setup can finish?",["The owner publishes it in the Microsoft 365 admin center","Permissions are granted automatically on Set up","A Global Administrator approves (consents to) the requested permissions","A Security Reader assigns the agent identity"],2,"Partner agents need tenant-wide admin consent for the permissions they request, which requires a Global Administrator."],["Where do you view a Copilot agent's required permissions and allow or block which agents are available in the organization?",["Entra admin center > Conditional Access","Microsoft 365 admin center > Integrated apps","Purview > Content search","Teams admin center"],1,"Integrated apps in the Microsoft 365 admin center centrally manages agents: view permissions, allow/block, control access. Conditional Access controls authentication, not agent availability."],["A maker publishes a custom agent at the ORGANIZATION level. What must happen before everyone can use it?",["Nothing, it's available immediately","Admin approval in the Microsoft 365 admin center","Approval in the Teams admin center","The maker downloads the publishing package"],1,"Org-wide agents must be approved by an admin in the Microsoft 365 admin center (Requested agents)."],["Compliance analysts must see WHERE sensitive info types are detected in Data/Content explorer but must NOT open or preview the files. Which role group?",["Content Explorer Content Viewer","Content Explorer List Viewer","Compliance Administrator","Security Administrator"],1,"List Viewer = see the list of locations only. Content Viewer = can also open the contents (too much)."],["What happens in the TRIAGE step of an Insider Risk Management workflow?",["Policy templates and risk indicators are configured","Alerts are evaluated and either dismissed, added to an existing case, or used to create a new case","The case is escalated to eDiscovery","HR connectors are installed"],1,"Triage = review alerts and decide: dismiss, add to case, or create case. Configuration happens earlier; eDiscovery escalation happens later."],["In an eDiscovery (Premium) review set, which feature identifies the most relevant content by detecting themes and near duplicates?",["Tags","Search statistics","Analytics","Legal hold"],2,"Analytics finds themes, groups similar documents and identifies near duplicates. Tags organize items after review."],["A user has an ELIGIBLE role assignment in PIM. What must happen before they can use the role's permissions?",["Nothing, eligible means active","The user activates the role (just-in-time)","An admin converts it to a permanent assignment","The user resets their password"],1,"Eligible assignments must be activated by the user, often with justification, MFA and approval, which gives just-in-time access."],["How is a Microsoft Copilot Studio license assigned?",["Per device","Per app","Per tenant","Per user"],3,"Copilot Studio licensing is assigned per user (granting tenant-wide rights to that user)."]]},{"t":"AB-900 Official Practice Assessment (50 Q)","d":"All 50 questions from the Microsoft practice assessment, with short explanations. Q1–16: core services & security · Q17–36: data protection & governance · Q37–50: Copilot & agent admin.","q":[["Which objects are configured in the Exchange admin center?",["SharePoint sites and document libraries","Mailboxes and distribution lists","Teams and channels","Conditional Access policies"],1,"Exchange admin center manages Exchange Online objects: mailboxes (incl. shared and resource) and mail-enabled groups such as distribution groups. Sites → SharePoint admin center, Teams → Teams admin center, Conditional Access → Entra."],["How are SharePoint Online site permissions granted to users?",["Add the users to a Microsoft Entra mail-enabled security group.","Assign the users the SharePoint Administrator role.","Add the users to a SharePoint group.","Make the users owners of a Microsoft 365 group."],2,"Site permissions come from SharePoint groups (Owners, Members, Visitors) tied to permission levels. SharePoint Administrator is a tenant-level admin role, not site content access."],["Admin1 must configure how users can access Microsoft 365 Copilot scenarios, following least privilege. Which role?",["Global Administrator","Global Reader","AI Administrator","Reports Reader"],2,"AI Administrator manages AI/Copilot settings without broad tenant privileges. Global Reader and Reports Reader are read-only."],["Where in the Microsoft 365 admin center can you add and manage custom domains?",["Settings > Org settings > Organization profile","Setup > Domains","Exchange admin center > Mail flow","Entra > Enterprise applications"],1,"Domains are added, verified and configured in the Domains area of the M365 admin center. Organization profile doesn't manage domains; Mail flow is email routing."],["In Microsoft 365, administrators manage mailboxes and distribution lists by using the ____.",["Microsoft Entra admin center","SharePoint admin center","Exchange admin center","Microsoft Teams admin center"],2,"Mailboxes and distribution lists are Exchange Online recipient objects."],["You can add a domain in the Microsoft 365 admin center by selecting ____.",["Reports","Billing","Health","Setup"],3,"Setup contains the add-domain workflow. Reports = usage, Billing = subscriptions, Health = service health and Message center."],["Which Microsoft Entra authentication method is passwordless?",["A FIDO2 passkey","A one-time SMS passcode","Voice call verification","A Temporary Access Pass"],0,"FIDO2 passkeys are phishing-resistant and passwordless. SMS and voice are weaker telephony methods; a Temporary Access Pass only bootstraps other methods."],["What is a core concept of the Zero Trust security model used in Microsoft 365?",["Automatically trust users on the corporate network.","Assume breach and verify every access request.","Grant permanent administrative permissions to IT staff.","Rely on passwords for authentication."],1,"Zero Trust assumes breach and continuously verifies identity, device health and permissions for every request."],["You need to apply Zero Trust by evaluating identity signals and automatically enforcing access policies. What should you implement?",["Intune device compliance policies","Intune app protection policies","Microsoft Defender Antivirus","Microsoft Entra Conditional Access"],3,"Conditional Access evaluates identity, device and risk signals at sign-in and enforces controls such as MFA or block."],["Which statement describes the 'Verify explicitly' Zero Trust principle?",["Trust domain-joined devices automatically.","Always authenticate and authorize based on all available data points.","Trust requests from the internal network.","Stop monitoring once MFA succeeds."],1,"Every request is authenticated and authorized using all signals: identity, device state, location and risk."],["Which statement accurately describes Microsoft Entra authorization?",["It proves who someone is by validating credentials.","It creates a single sign-on session across applications.","It provides the access level and allowed actions.","It encrypts data at rest."],2,"Authorization = what a verified identity can access and do. Validating credentials and SSO relate to authentication."],["What is the purpose of multifactor authentication (MFA)?",["Automatically assign roles and permissions.","Provide an additional verification factor during sign-in.","Encrypt data at rest.","Let users access many apps after one sign-in."],1,"MFA adds a factor (app notification, hardware key, code) on top of the password."],["The ____ Zero Trust principle requires designing security controls with the expectation that attackers might already be inside.",["Trust the network perimeter","Use shared credentials","Assume breach","Verify after sign-in"],2,"Assume breach drives segmentation, monitoring and limiting blast radius."],["What is the primary benefit of single sign-on (SSO)?",["Automatically assigns administrative roles.","Encrypts data at rest across Microsoft 365.","Requires users to reauthenticate for each app.","Users sign in once and access authorized apps without signing in again."],3,"SSO = one sign-in with Entra ID, then access to multiple authorized apps."],["What is the purpose of Identity Secure Score improvement actions in Microsoft Entra?",["To provide recommendations that help increase the identity security posture","To automatically enforce Conditional Access policies","To generate security alerts","To predict the probability of a future breach"],0,"Improvement actions are recommendations (e.g. enable MFA, block legacy auth) that raise the score when implemented. They don't enforce anything automatically."],["What is required before a user with an ELIGIBLE role assignment can use the privileged role in PIM?",["An administrator activates it automatically","Activation of the role by the user","Converting the assignment to active","Nothing, eligible gives permanent access"],1,"Eligible users must activate the role themselves, which gives just-in-time access with no standing privilege."],["What is a primary use case for Microsoft Purview sensitivity labels?",["Provide SSO for applications","Detect compromised accounts","Classify content and apply protections","Route traffic through VPN tunnels"],2,"Labels classify and protect content with encryption, markings and access restrictions."],["You need to control how long user prompts and responses for AI apps are retained before they are deleted automatically. Which Purview feature?",["Sensitive information types (SITs)","DLP policies","Sensitivity labels","Retention policies"],3,"Retention policies (Data Lifecycle Management) retain or delete content, including supported AI prompts and responses. SITs only identify patterns."],["How do Microsoft Purview sensitivity labels protect data after it has been classified?",["They track user actions such as sharing events.","They identify patterns such as credit card numbers.","They persist with content wherever it is stored or shared.","They restrict sharing across Microsoft 365 locations."],2,"Protection travels with the content. Patterns = SITs, restricting sharing = DLP, tracking actions = auditing."],["What is the purpose of a Microsoft Purview retention policy?",["To detect risky user behavior","To control how long content is stored and when it is deleted","To classify and encrypt content","To prevent sensitive data from leaving the organization"],1,"Risky behavior → Insider Risk; classify/encrypt → sensitivity labels; prevent leaving → DLP."],["How can Microsoft Purview retention settings affect content lifespan?",["Encrypt the content when it ages.","Block external sharing after a period.","Require users to archive content manually.","Retain the content for a defined period, and then delete it."],3,"Retention keeps content for a set period and can then delete it automatically."],["Microsoft Purview ____ are used to prevent sensitive information from being shared outside a company.",["retention labels","sensitivity labels","data loss prevention (DLP) policies","sharing policies"],2,"DLP detects sensitive info and blocks external sharing across Exchange, SharePoint and OneDrive."],["Microsoft Purview ____ can be used to find sensitive data in user prompts and responses when users interact with AI apps.",["DLP policies","sensitive information types (SITs) and trainable classifiers","eDiscovery cases and review sets","retention policies and labels"],1,"Classification (SITs and trainable classifiers) FINDS sensitive data, including in AI prompts. DLP enforces after detection."],["Which statement accurately describes Microsoft responsible AI principles for agents and generative AI?",["They include fairness, transparency, and accountability.","They guarantee AI outputs are always accurate.","They require storing all prompts for investigation.","They let agents bypass RBAC when needed."],0,"The six principles: fairness, reliability & safety, privacy & security, inclusiveness, transparency, accountability."],["You need Copilot Control System to monitor, detect, and respond to risks related to Copilot and agent use. Which type of controls?",["Compliance and privacy controls","Data security controls","Management controls","AI security controls"],3,"'Monitor, detect, respond' = AI security controls. Compliance/privacy = regulations; management = operational governance."],["The security team receives a Purview DLP alert. Which tool should you use to review detailed user activity related to the alert?",["Content explorer","Data explorer","Activity explorer","Microsoft Purview Audit"],2,"Activity explorer shows user actions tied to DLP and labels. Content explorer shows where sensitive data lives; Audit is broader logging."],["What does Compliance Manager provide to assess generative AI apps against frameworks such as the EU AI Act and NIST AI RMF?",["Capturing Copilot prompts in the unified audit log","DLP enforcement for prompts that contain sensitive data","Oversharing assessments for SharePoint sites","Regulatory templates to assess and track compliance controls"],3,"Compliance Manager = regulatory templates and assessments."],["Compliance analysts must use Data explorer to see where SITs are detected but must NOT open or preview file contents. Which role group?",["Content Explorer List Viewer","Content Explorer Content Viewer","Compliance Administrator","Security Administrator"],0,"List Viewer = aggregated locations only. Content Viewer can open contents, which is too much."],["What is the primary purpose of the TRIAGE step in Insider Risk Management?",["Define risk indicators by configuring policy templates","Evaluate alerts and decide to create a case, add to a case, or dismiss","Synthesize alerts and user details during investigation","Escalate cases to eDiscovery"],1,"Triage = review alerts and decide: dismiss, add to existing case, or create a new case."],["You have an eDiscovery case with a review set and need to identify the most relevant content. What should you use?",["Predictive coding models","Search statistics","Tags","Analytics"],3,"Analytics detects themes, groups similar documents and identifies near duplicates. Tags organize items after review."],["You plan to implement Copilot and need to discover how users interact with generative AI tools and identify data exposure risks. What should you use?",["Microsoft Purview DLP","DSPM for AI","Data Lifecycle Management","eDiscovery"],1,"DSPM for AI provides visibility into AI usage and exposure risks. DLP only prevents inappropriate sharing."],["You need to identify unusual or potentially risky file access activity in SharePoint Online. What should you use?",["Data access governance reports","Microsoft Defender for Office 365 reports","Session summary reports","User risk assessment reports"],2,"Session summary reports surface activity anomalies. DAG reports focus on oversharing exposure; Defender for Office 365 on email threats; user risk on identity."],["You plan to implement Copilot and need to identify potential oversharing in SharePoint and OneDrive sites. What should you use?",["Site access reviews","Change history reports","Restricted Content Discovery","Data access governance reports"],3,"DAG reports give tenant-wide oversharing insight. Site access reviews cover one site; Restricted Content Discovery hides content but doesn't identify oversharing."],["You run a 'Sharing links' Data access governance report. Which insight does it provide?",["Large files stored in SharePoint","Sites where the most sharing links were created during the last 28 days","SharePoint sign-in activity","Users who created the most SharePoint sites"],1,"It highlights sites with the most sharing links in the last 28 days."],["To identify potential oversharing for SharePoint and OneDrive, you can use ____ in the Microsoft Purview portal.",["Compliance Manager assessments","DLP alerts","data risk assessments","eDiscovery (Standard) cases"],2,"Data risk assessments (in DSPM) analyze permissions and exposure. In the SharePoint admin center the equivalent is DAG reports."],["To limit a SharePoint site's access to only users in specified Microsoft 365 or Entra security groups, use ____ in the SharePoint admin center.",["restricted access control","data access governance reports","a block download policy","site access reviews"],0,"Restricted access control enforces group-based site access. DAG reports discover; block download limits unmanaged devices; access reviews remediate."],["You need a custom agent that uses content in files, folders and SharePoint sites and can be shared in Teams chats and meetings. What should you use?",["Copilot in OneDrive","SharePoint agents","Copilot in SharePoint","Copilot Prompt Gallery"],1,"SharePoint agents use SharePoint content as knowledge and can be shared in Teams. The prompt gallery stores prompts, not agents."],["You need an agent that automatically runs multi-step workflows in external systems, with custom orchestration and custom AI models. Which type?",["Declarative agent","Security Copilot Phishing Triage Agent","SharePoint agent","Custom engine agent"],3,"Custom engine agents = custom orchestration, external systems, custom models. Declarative agents use M365 data with built-in orchestration."],["What is a key difference between a Copilot license and pay-as-you-go for scenarios that retrieve SharePoint data?",["The Copilot license includes Copilot capabilities, while pay-as-you-go can incur usage-based charges for data retrieval and API usage.","Pay-as-you-go requires every user to also have a Copilot license.","The Copilot license only works in web-based chat.","Pay-as-you-go includes all Copilot app experiences at no extra cost."],0,"License = built-in Copilot capabilities across apps. PAYG = consumption billing for extensibility like data retrieval and APIs, and can be used alongside licenses."],["You need to integrate a custom AI assistant into Microsoft 365 that supports complex workflows, custom business logic and external system integration. What should you use?",["A declarative agent","Copilot connectors","A custom engine agent","Copilot plugins"],2,"Connectors bring data in; plugins add actions; declarative agents use built-in orchestration. Complex custom logic = custom engine agent."],["Declarative agents use Microsoft 365 data and built-in orchestration, while custom engine agents ____.",["use only Microsoft 365 data sources","support custom orchestration and integration with external systems","use only built-in orchestration","work only inside Teams chats"],1,"'Only M365 data / only built-in orchestration' describes declarative agents."],["What provides the Copilot Dashboard and the Advanced Insights Analyst Workbench?",["Microsoft 365 admin center usage reports","Microsoft Purview audit logs","Power Platform and Copilot Studio analytics","Viva Insights Copilot Analytics"],3,"Viva Insights Copilot Analytics provides both. Power Platform analytics cover custom agents, not org-wide Copilot adoption."],["Which Entra role can access Copilot > Billing & usage in the M365 admin center and configure pay-as-you-go billing for agents?",["Exchange Administrator","AI Administrator","SharePoint Administrator","Teams Administrator"],1,"AI Administrator manages the Copilot node, including PAYG billing."],["Which user-scoping options are available when creating a pay-as-you-go billing policy?",["A specific group only","All users or specific users","All users or a specific group","Up to 1,000 specific users"],2,"All users or a specific Entra security group. Individual accounts aren't a scoping option."],["You need to delete multiple scheduled prompts created by a user in Microsoft 365 Copilot. What should you do FIRST?",["Run Connect-AzAccount","Install the required PowerShell modules","Assign the Power Platform Administrator role to your account","Run the Clear-CopilotActions script"],2,"Scheduled prompts live in a Power Platform environment, so the role comes first and the scripts after."],["You can assign a Microsoft Copilot Studio license as a ____ license.",["per app","per device","per tenant","per user"],3,"Copilot Studio is licensed per user."],["A maker publishes a custom agent at the organizational level. What must occur before it becomes available organization-wide?",["It becomes available automatically.","The agent must be submitted for approval in the Microsoft 365 admin center.","An admin approves it in the Teams admin center.","The maker downloads and tests the publishing package."],1,"Org-scoped agents require admin approval in the M365 admin center."],["In Agent Builder, you need the agent to answer questions using content from specific organizational resources. What should you do?",["Define the agent's description.","Define the agent's instructions.","Add a knowledge source to the agent.","Enable capabilities."],2,"Knowledge sources ground answers in specific content. Instructions shape behavior; capabilities add tools like the code interpreter."],["A Security Copilot owner configures a partner-built agent that requests permissions to Microsoft services. What must occur before setup can complete?",["A global administrator must approve the required permissions.","The owner must publish the agent in the M365 admin center.","Permissions are granted automatically on Set up.","A Security Reader assigns the agent identity to a user."],0,"Tenant-wide permissions for partner agents need Global Administrator consent."],["You need to restrict which users can access a specific Copilot agent. Where can you view the agent's required permissions and control which agents are allowed?",["Entra admin center > Conditional Access","Purview > Content search","Teams admin center","Microsoft 365 admin center > Integrated apps"],3,"Integrated apps centrally manages agents: permissions, allow/block and access."]]},{"t":"AB-900 Official Bank: New Questions (Round 2)","d":"The 24 new questions from the second Microsoft practice assessment attempt, with short explanations.","q":[["Which SharePoint Online objects are used to organize and store content?",["Users, licenses, and mailboxes","Sites, libraries, and folders","Teams, channels, and chats","Tenants, subscriptions, and domains"],1,"Sites, libraries and folders are SharePoint's content containers. Tenants, subscriptions and domains are administrative constructs."],["Licenses are assigned by group-based licensing. What happens when a user is removed from the licensed group?",["The licenses remain until manually removed.","The licenses convert to direct user-assigned licenses.","The licenses assigned through the group are removed from the user.","The user keeps access but stops consuming a license."],2,"Entra ID automatically removes group-assigned licenses when membership ends; assignment and removal are both automated."],["Which Microsoft 365 object grants permissions to multiple users at once and simplifies access management?",["Distribution list","Shared mailbox","Teams channel","Security group"],3,"Security groups assign permissions to many users at once. Distribution lists are for email only."],["In Microsoft 365 you can investigate security alerts and incidents by using the ____.",["Microsoft 365 admin center","Microsoft Entra admin center","Microsoft Defender portal","Microsoft Purview portal"],2,"The Defender portal has the unified incident queue that correlates alerts from multiple security services. Purview = compliance; Entra = identity."],["What is the purpose of making a user ELIGIBLE for a privileged role in PIM?",["To grant permanent administrative permissions","To automatically assign Global Admin for emergencies","To provide just-in-time, time-bound role activation","To replace Conditional Access policies for sign-in risk"],2,"Eligible = activate only when needed, time-limited, optionally with approval, justification and MFA."],["Which TWO settings must be configured in every Microsoft Entra Conditional Access policy?",["Locations and Device compliance status","Users or agents, and Target resources","Target resources and Locations","Users or agents, and Device compliance status"],1,"Every policy needs WHO (users or agents) and WHAT (target resources). Locations and device compliance are optional conditions."],["A user reports that sign-in required MFA. You need to find out which Conditional Access policy required it. What should you use?",["Exchange message trace","Microsoft Entra Sign-in diagnostics","Microsoft Purview audit logs","Teams Call analytics"],1,"Sign-in diagnostics analyzes authentication events and gives guidance for MFA and Conditional Access issues."],["You need to apply Purview sensitivity labels to ON-PREMISES files that contain sensitive information. What should you use?",["A Purview DLP policy","Microsoft Purview Information Protection scanner","An eDiscovery search","An Insider Risk Management policy"],1,"The scanner discovers sensitive data in on-prem file shares and SharePoint Server and applies labels."],["Which Microsoft Purview solution can you use to discover and label sensitive files?",["Data Lifecycle Management","Data loss prevention","DSPM for AI","Microsoft Purview Information Protection"],3,"Information Protection discovers, classifies and labels. DSPM for AI focuses on AI-related risk, not labeling files."],["How does Microsoft 365 Copilot access Microsoft 365 data?",["It retrieves all tenant data for licensed users.","It uses a service account that bypasses Entra authorization.","It retrieves only data that the user is authorized to access.","It uses an index that ignores access controls."],2,"The golden rule: Copilot works within the user's identity and permission context."],["What is the role of Microsoft Graph in Microsoft 365 Copilot responses?",["It validates Microsoft 365 licenses before prompts are processed.","It encrypts prompts.","It stores Copilot responses in a data warehouse.","It retrieves organizational context, such as files, emails, and meetings."],3,"Graph grounds Copilot in tenant content: files, emails, meetings, chats, calendar."],["How does Microsoft Defender help protect Microsoft 365 Copilot interactions?",["It analyzes Copilot prompts for security threats and suspicious activity.","It encrypts Copilot responses.","It replaces Entra authentication.","It stores prompts for long-term retention."],0,"Defender = threat detection. Encryption = Information Protection; authentication = Entra; retention = Purview."],["You deploy Microsoft 365 Copilot. Which PAIR of statements correctly describes how Copilot uses company data?",["Prompts train foundation models; data protection applies only to web queries.","Prompts and responses are not used to train foundation models, and they are protected the same way as emails and files.","Prompts are shared with other tenants; responses are not stored.","Enterprise data protection applies only to custom agents."],1,"No training of foundation models, and prompts and responses get the same protection as other Microsoft 365 data. Enterprise data protection applies broadly, including web queries and agents."],["Which responsible AI principle focuses on treating users equitably and minimizing bias in outcomes?",["Accountability","Inclusiveness","Fairness","Transparency"],2,"Fairness = equity and minimal bias. Inclusiveness = works for people with diverse needs and abilities. Transparency = open about how it works. Accountability = humans remain responsible."],["Microsoft 365 Copilot uses Microsoft Graph to retrieve context such as ____.",["only SharePoint metadata","only user authentication tokens","only external connector data","files, emails, meetings, and chats"],3,"Graph aggregates signals from many Microsoft 365 services, not just one source."],["What does DSPM for AI do to help discover and manage AI activity and related data risks?",["Automatically labels all Copilot-accessed files","Disables non-Microsoft AI services by default","Provides visibility into AI activity and identifies potential data exposure risks","Encrypts prompts with customer-managed keys"],2,"DSPM for AI = visibility + risk identification + recommendations."],["You must ensure that ONLY users in a specific group can access a SharePoint site and its content. What should you use?",["Restricted Content Discovery","Restricted Access Control","An inactive site policy","A site access review"],1,"Restricted Access Control limits access to a group. Restricted Content Discovery only hides content from search and Copilot WITHOUT changing permissions."],["Which scenario is most appropriate for the Researcher agent?",["Create a short status update from a Teams chat","Provide a quick brainstorming list for a meeting agenda","Perform multi-step research and produce a cited report","Summarize an email thread"],2,"Researcher gathers from web and org content over multiple steps and produces a structured, source-cited report. Quick tasks fit standard Copilot."],["What is a key difference between Microsoft 365 Copilot Chat and Microsoft 365 Copilot built-in capabilities?",["Copilot Chat is a standalone chat experience, while Microsoft 365 Copilot is integrated into apps like Word and Excel.","Copilot Chat can never use work data.","Microsoft 365 Copilot is chat-only.","There is no difference."],0,"Chat = standalone (browser/mobile); Microsoft 365 Copilot = integrated in apps. Chat can use work data in enterprise scenarios."],["In the Copilot usage report in the M365 admin center, which metric shows the number of users LICENSED for Copilot?",["Active Users","Active agent users","Adoption by app","Enabled Users"],3,"Enabled = licensed. Active = actually used Copilot in the period."],["During a phased rollout, you need to assign Copilot licenses to a pilot group. What should you use?",["Power Platform admin center","Microsoft Purview portal","Microsoft 365 admin center","Microsoft Entra admin center"],2,"Per Microsoft's assessment, Copilot licenses are assigned in the M365 admin center; Entra lets you review them but not assign."],["After you assign Microsoft 365 Copilot licenses to users, ____.",["users must wait exactly 24 hours","Copilot appears in Word and Excel","Copilot appears in PowerPoint and Visio","users must request access from IT"],1,"Copilot becomes available in supported apps (Word, Excel, PowerPoint, Outlook, Teams). Visio isn't a standard Copilot app here."],["In the Agent Registry inventory in the M365 admin center, what does the 'Risks' column represent?",["Total active alerts across all severities","Active high-severity alerts for the agent and its instances","The number of blocked agents","Pending update approvals"],1,"Risks = active HIGH-severity alerts only (not medium or low)."],["A developer submits a custom agent, but users report they can't access it. What is the most likely reason?",["It must be indexed in Microsoft Search first.","It needs a sensitivity label.","It must be added to a DLP policy.","It is waiting for administrator review and approval."],3,"Org agents need admin approval before users can access them."]]},{"t":"AB-900 Official Bank: New Questions (Round 3)","d":"The 13 new questions from the third Microsoft practice assessment attempt.","q":[["Where in the Microsoft Teams admin center can you configure whether users can create private or shared channels?",["Meetings > Meeting policies","Teams > Teams policies","Teams > Manage teams","Users > Manage users"],1,"Teams policies control whether users can create private and shared channels. Meeting policies apply to meeting features, Manage teams manages individual teams, and user settings manage accounts."],["Which statement accurately describes a key capability of Microsoft Defender XDR?",["It is a compliance portal for audit log searches and retention policies.","It is used to create and publish sensitivity labels.","It correlates threat signals to detect attacks and support automated investigation and response (AIR).","It is used to configure device compliance and Conditional Access policies."],2,"Defender XDR correlates signals across endpoints, identities, email and apps and supports AIR. Audit and retention = Purview; sensitivity labels = Purview Information Protection; device compliance and CA = Intune and Entra."],["Your company uses Microsoft 365 Copilot. Which security control restricts user access to Copilot?",["Microsoft Purview retention policies","Microsoft Sentinel analytics rules","Microsoft Entra Conditional Access policies","SharePoint storage quotas"],2,"Conditional Access enforces identity-based access controls (MFA, device compliance, location) before users can reach Copilot. Retention = data lifecycle; Sentinel analytics rules = detection; storage quotas = storage."],["What does the identity secure score percentage indicate in Microsoft Entra ID?",["The number of identity-related incidents detected by Defender during the last 24 hours","How closely the identity security configuration aligns with Microsoft recommended best practices","The percentage of users blocked by Conditional Access policies","The predicted likelihood of a breach within a specific timeframe"],1,"Identity Secure Score measures alignment with Microsoft's recommended identity practices and rises as you complete improvement actions such as enabling MFA."],["To review user activity across Microsoft 365 services, you can use ____.",["Microsoft Defender activity logs","Microsoft Entra sign-in logs","Microsoft Purview Audit","the Microsoft Teams admin center"],2,"Purview Audit is the centralized audit log across Exchange, SharePoint, Teams and more. Entra sign-in logs only cover sign-ins; Defender logs focus on security events."],["Which statement accurately describes Microsoft Purview data classification for AI?",["Data classification automatically encrypts Copilot prompts and responses.","Data classification blocks Copilot access to SharePoint and OneDrive content.","Data classification applies only to Exchange.","Data classification identifies sensitive data by using sensitive information types (SITs) and classifiers."],3,"Classification FINDS sensitive data with SITs and trainable classifiers, across many services and AI interactions. It doesn't encrypt or block anything by itself."],["Which Microsoft responsible AI principle focuses on being open about how an AI system works and what it can do?",["Accountability","Inclusiveness","Fairness","Transparency"],3,"Transparency = open about how it works and what it can do. Accountability = humans stay responsible; fairness = no bias; inclusiveness = works for diverse needs."],["In Microsoft Purview Activity explorer, you can ____ how labeled content is accessed, modified, and shared.",["encrypt","monitor","restore","quarantine"],1,"Activity explorer MONITORS activity on sensitive and labeled content. It doesn't encrypt, restore or quarantine files."],["Which Data access governance report in the SharePoint admin center helps track oversharing activities that occurred during the last 28 days?",["A snapshot report","An activity report","The Sensitivity label for files report","The Site permissions for users report"],1,"Activity reports show sharing and access activity from the last 28 days. Snapshot reports are a point-in-time view of permissions."],["You are evaluating the built-in Microsoft 365 Copilot agents. What is the purpose of the Analyst agent?",["To configure retention labels and eDiscovery cases","To enforce Conditional Access policies","To analyze data by using natural language prompts","To provision SharePoint Online sites and manage site permissions"],2,"Analyst analyzes datasets with natural language and produces insights, trends and visualizations. The other options are Purview, Entra and SharePoint admin tasks."],["You need to prevent users from accessing the Word, Excel, and PowerPoint agents in Microsoft 365 Copilot. What removes them from the Tools menu and the agent navigation pane?",["Block Bing Web Search for Microsoft 365 Copilot","Disable the Anthropic AI models connection in the Microsoft 365 admin center","Disable Copilot Tuning","Remove the Microsoft 365 Copilot license"],1,"These agents rely on the Anthropic AI models connection, so disabling it removes them. Bing affects web grounding, Tuning affects customization, and removing the license disables Copilot entirely."],["Which Microsoft 365 role provides the minimum permissions required to configure, manage, and deploy Copilot agents?",["Compliance Administrator","Security Reader","AI Administrator","Teams Administrator"],2,"AI Administrator manages Copilot features and agents. Compliance Admin = retention/eDiscovery; Security Reader = read-only; Teams Admin = Teams."],["You need a centralized dashboard to review agent adoption, usage trends, alerts, and governance gaps across a tenant. What should you use?",["Agent Registry in the Microsoft 365 admin center","The Microsoft Entra admin center","Operational health in the Power Platform admin center","Agent Overview in the Microsoft 365 admin center"],3,"Agent Overview = the monitoring dashboard (adoption, trends, alerts, governance). Agent Registry = inventory and management. PPAC operational health = service and environment health."]]},{"t":"AB-900 Official Bank: New Questions (Round 4)","d":"The 6 new questions from the fourth Microsoft practice assessment attempt.","q":[["What is a difference between app registrations and enterprise applications in Microsoft Entra ID?",["App registrations are used only for Entra App Gallery applications, while enterprise applications are used only for non-gallery applications.","App registrations define the application identity and authentication settings, while enterprise applications represent the tenant instance used to manage access.","Conditional Access policies are configured within app registrations.","App registrations and enterprise applications are identical objects."],1,"App registration = the app's identity and auth config (redirect URIs, credentials, API permissions). Enterprise application (service principal) = the tenant instance where you manage access: user assignments, SSO and sign-in monitoring."],["You need users to be prompted for MFA when a high-risk sign-in is detected. What should you use?",["A Microsoft Entra access review","Security defaults","A Microsoft Entra Conditional Access policy","An Exchange mail flow rule"],2,"Risk-based Conditional Access uses Entra ID Protection risk signals to require MFA. Access reviews periodically review access; security defaults can't be configured for risk; mail flow rules don't control authentication."],["Which Microsoft 365 workloads can return results in Microsoft Purview eDiscovery when you search for files and email messages?",["Windows Server file shares, on-premises Exchange Server, and SQL Server databases","Azure DevOps repositories, GitHub repositories, and Intune device inventory","Microsoft Teams, Exchange Online, SharePoint Online, and OneDrive for Business","Microsoft Entra ID and Azure Key Vault"],2,"eDiscovery searches Microsoft 365 cloud workloads: Exchange Online, SharePoint Online, OneDrive and Teams. On-prem systems, code repositories and identity/secret stores aren't eDiscovery locations."],["What occurs in Microsoft Purview Communication Compliance when a message matches a policy condition?",["The message is deleted automatically.","The message is encrypted automatically by using a sensitivity label.","The message is moved automatically to an eDiscovery case.","The message appears on the Pending tab for review."],3,"Matching messages are flagged onto the Pending tab for human reviewers. Nothing is deleted, encrypted or moved to eDiscovery automatically."],["Your company is rolling out Microsoft 365 Copilot. You need to identify SharePoint and OneDrive locations that might contain overshared content. What should you use in the Microsoft Purview portal?",["Microsoft Purview Data Catalog","Microsoft Purview Data Map","Data risk assessments in Data Security Posture Management (DSPM)","Self-help diagnostics in the Help pane"],2,"Data risk assessments in DSPM find overshared content before a broad Copilot rollout. Data Catalog and Data Map manage data assets and lineage; Help pane diagnostics troubleshoot service issues."],["A company will use Copilot extensibility features that retrieve data from SharePoint Online. What is a difference between the monthly Copilot add-on license and pay-as-you-go?",["Pay-as-you-go enables OneDrive retrieval through APIs, but the monthly license does not.","Pay-as-you-go is required to use SharePoint agents.","The monthly Copilot license includes Copilot capabilities, while pay-as-you-go can charge for data retrieval from sources.","The monthly license is billed per API call, while pay-as-you-go is a fixed fee."],2,"Monthly license = core Copilot capabilities. PAYG = consumption billing for extensibility such as data retrieval and APIs. PAYG isn't required for SharePoint agents, and both models can access M365 data."]]},{"t":"AB-900 Official Bank: New Questions (Round 5)","d":"The 5 new questions from the fifth Microsoft practice assessment attempt.","q":[["Microsoft Defender for Office 365 helps protect users from ____.",["device compliance violations","phishing attacks","insider risk activities","unauthorized sign-ins"],1,"Defender for Office 365 protects email and collaboration: phishing, malicious links and malware in messages and files. Device compliance = Intune; insider risk = Insider Risk Management; unauthorized sign-ins = Entra ID Protection and sign-in monitoring."],["You plan to use Microsoft 365 Copilot to access data stored in THIRD-PARTY systems. Copilot must only retrieve data that users are authorized to access. What should Copilot use?",["Microsoft Graph","An agent","A connector","A prompt"],2,"Copilot connectors index external content while respecting the source system's permissions. Graph covers Microsoft 365 data; agents extend Copilot but don't connect data sources; prompts are user input."],["What is the primary purpose of running the Sharing links Data access governance report when investigating potential oversharing?",["Identify sites that contain files with specific sensitivity labels","List all the sites a specified user can access and whether access is direct or through group membership","Identify sites where users created the most new sharing links during the last 28 days","Provide a snapshot of permissions across all sites"],2,"Sharing links report = sites with the most new sharing links in the last 28 days. Listing a user's sites = the user access report; labels = classification tools; permission snapshot = snapshot reports."],["You need to review the prompts that a specific user saved, liked, or shared in Copilot Prompt Gallery. What should you use?",["Create a Microsoft Purview eDiscovery case","Review Microsoft 365 usage reports","Export the user's prompts from Copilot Prompt Gallery by using PowerShell","Run a Microsoft Purview audit log search"],2,"A PowerShell export retrieves the actual saved, liked or shared prompts for one user. Usage reports are aggregated; audit logs capture events, not prompt content; eDiscovery is for legal investigations."],["You need to configure which users can access Microsoft 365 Copilot agents. Which Copilot Control System setting in the Microsoft 365 admin center should you use?",["Data security","Overview","Settings","Data access"],3,"Data access configures which users and groups can access agents and their data sources. Data security = protecting sensitive info; Overview = dashboard; Settings = general Copilot feature options."]]}];
